span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">quotedValue</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myQuoteExpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">res</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">res</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkApp2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Quoted.unsafeMk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">quotedTy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">quotedValue</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">debug</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Result: {res}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">res</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myq</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- q(1 + 1) : Q(Nat)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>But there's a problem: when we quote a metavariable that never gets assigned, instead of getting a helpful error message, we get:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">PANIC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reportStuckSyntheticMVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SyntheticMVars</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">316</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">11</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unreachable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">code</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">been</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reached</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Clearly something is not so unreachable here! The problem is that the <code>reportStuckSyntheticMVar</code> function doesn't know which error to report for our special Qq metavariables -- I'd prefer <em>none</em>, since the Qq metavariable is only a proxy for the actual problematic metavariable that we already would get an error for, so perhaps it would be good to change that <code>unreachable!</code> into a <code>pure ()</code>. On the other hand, I might be abusing synthetic metavariables here, maybe anyone knows something better we can do instead. Thoughts?</p>",
